{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgXF9B9G6faGrSZKNM2RR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The study ran end to end, and three of the four parts of the hypothesis did not hold as stated. The biggest surprise is that whitespace changes disturb models more than punctuation changes, not less.\n\n**Setup:** there was no API key on this host and no pre-gathered papers, datasets or code. So I used 11 open models: five Qwen2.5 (0.5B–14B), three Llama-3.x (1B, 3B, 8B) and three Qwen3 (0.6B, 4B, 8B). Qwen3-8B ran on the local Qwen3-8B server; the rest are mostly 4-bit quantized. Tasks were three classification sets (SST-2, AG News, BoolQ; 1,200 items) and two code sets (HumanEval, MBPP; 464 problems). Each item ran under the original prompt, a byte-identical re-run as a noise floor, and 10 formatting changes, all with greedy decoding: about 220k generations, $0 cost.\n\n| Hypothesis | Result | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| Formatting flips labels 5–15% | 4.9% (CI 4.6–5.1%), vs 0.02% for the identical re-run; significant in 80 of 110 model × change cells | Borderline, just under the range: small models are inside it, larger ones below |\n| Whitespace 3–8%, punctuation 8–20% | Whitespace 7.1%, punctuation 2.2%; whitespace is worse in every model | Whitespace range holds, but the ordering is **reversed** |\n| Models under 3B are 2–3× more sensitive | 2.2× for classification (CI 2.0–2.4); no size effect on code | Supported for classification only |\n| Code most affected, 15–25% | Code text changes in 36% of problems, but pass/fail changes in only 5.1%, about the same as label flips | Depends on the metric |\n\n- **Why whitespace is worse:** double spaces and no-break spaces change how every word is tokenized. But whitespace stays more disruptive when the number of changed tokens is matched. A single trailing blank line flips 3.4% of labels, versus 1.3% for swapping in proper dashes.\n- **Placebo check:** Llama's chat template strips trailing newlines, so that change produces identical tokens and exactly 0 flips. Whether a change matters depends on the serving template as well as the model.\n- **Accuracy hardly moves:** flips go in both directions and land mostly on items the model already gets wrong, so net accuracy changes stay within about ±1 point (one exception, Llama-3.2-1B, loses 2.8 on whitespace).\n- **Code noise floor:** re-running an identical code prompt in a different batch position already changes the generated code 6% of the time. Without that control, about a sixth of the code effect would be wrongly blamed on formatting.\n- **Replication:** re-running Qwen2.5-0.5B in a separate engine on another GPU reproduced all 19,968 outputs exactly.\n\n**Limitations:**\n- No commercial models were tested.\n- Each task uses only one prompt template.\n- Some small models give near-constant answers, which understates their sensitivity. For example, Llama-3.2-1B answers \"no\" to 95% of BoolQ and Qwen3-0.6B labels 80% of AG News \"sports\".\n- The ellipsis change applies to very few items.\n- The related-work section relies on my background knowledge, not papers gathered for this run.\n\nI also added a memory note on how to hand a GPU slice between worker processes without losing it on this shared host.\n\nEverything is in the workspace: `REPORT.md` has the full write-up with tables, figures and limitations, and `README.md` has an overview and how to reproduce."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1245,"cache_read_input_tokens":245884,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1245},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ca68dff7-3fed-493e-b883-6ab7358c4498","uuid":"8bcee676-01a7-42cc-b0d0-454491e8e246","timestamp":"2026-10-29T21:33:20.662Z","request_id":"req_011CgXF9AstWmrdPZbmUjqjk"}
